        "description": "Asked which Enigma model was most widely deployed in WWII, how many rotors Enigma I had, and whether the naval M3 was compatible with it (2023/05/20). Enigma I was the widely deployed German Army and Air Force model and always used three installed rotors, selected from a set that grew from three to five. The naval M3 also used three installed rotors and had three additional naval-only rotor choices (VI–VIII). It could interoperate with Enigma I using shared rotors and matching reflector, ring, starting-position, and plugboard settings; this did not make all naval configurations compatible. The four-rotor model was the naval M4, not a later Enigma I. The earlier claim that M3 used more complex plugboard wiring was misleading."
