        "title": "Nmap timing and host discovery options",
        "description": "Asked what `-T`, `-sL`, and `-P0` mean (2023/04/03). `-T0` through `-T5` select timing templates from slowest to fastest; `-T3` (normal), not `-T2` (polite), is the default. `-sL` lists targets without testing whether they are up; add `-n` to suppress DNS lookups. `-P0` is old syntax for `-Pn`, which skips host discovery and treats targets as up for scanning."
      }
